<p>Danish authorities in January prepared military contingency measures in Greenland after President Trump threatened to take over the Arctic territory, according to reports citing a military operations order reviewed by Danish public broadcaster DR. The disclosures suggest Copenhagen treated the threat as a real security scenario and quietly planned for a potential Arctic crisis involving the US. Separate reports said the preparations included extra personnel and emergency supplies for Greenland, underscoring how seriously Denmark took the episode despite its alliance with Washington.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/s9Wn3jL7SF-S2fBdteGSnLvTClK_z5_KTF1NZF7J7jgS-feFkHXV8DM5mxLgPx7zIU8U_N9z6BOGieljg-wFhS0xaIhCflZwjN9JyBza3pyPyI0KFtpBlFSnsUj3MP-XUQXzekhNY3IuKIESQ8aQTHFsx6eCHUS09xyxK9VtVCzo1Ey1bQum7yMS_kAzbPvbg-kwztXVwCI5oQ8W6jD3CQ93CuSeD9G4a8MPc8s5m7xAq0mu-EaMMg7Qs26MGJahQqz5-XLIV6VZqFSPzIc9' alt='Image accompanying Guardian coverage of Denmark’s reported Greenland contingency planning' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Threat language: The Guardian said Denmark’s planning unfolded during the days when Trump threatened to take Greenland “the hard way,” helping explain why Copenhagen treated the episode as more than rhetoric.</li><li>Medical planning: The FT and Guardian reported that Denmark sent blood supplies to Greenland, suggesting planners were preparing for possible combat casualties rather than a purely symbolic deployment.</li><li>Runway contingency: The FT and Guardian said Denmark also sent explosives for possible runway demolition if US forces invaded, showing planners considered ways to slow or hinder an assault on the island.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Danish military planners: The reported order suggests Copenhagen moved from political alarm to operational defense planning for Greenland once Trump’s threats escalated. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/19/denmark-deployed-troops-to-greenland-in-january-fearing-us-invasion-local-media-report'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Danish public broadcaster DR: By saying it had seen a dated operations order, DR presented the episode as documented contingency planning rather than a rumor about general unease in Copenhagen. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/19/denmark-prepared-for-us-attack-donald-trump-greenland'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Financial Times: The FT focused on the practical scope of the contingency, highlighting medical supplies and a runway-demolition option as signs that Denmark was preparing for a possible clash, not just signaling resolve. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e0783399-613f-4432-87a3-262698f3f6ca'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1rxzean/denmark_considered_destroying_greenland_runways/'>Denmark considered destroying Greenland runways amid fears of US attack</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/19/denmark-deployed-troops-to-greenland-in-january-fearing-us-invasion-local-media-report'>Denmark deployed troops to Greenland in January fearing US invasion, local media report</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e0783399-613f-4432-87a3-262698f3f6ca'>Denmark was ready to blow up Greenland runways if US invaded</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/19/denmark-prepared-for-us-attack-donald-trump-greenland'>Denmark reportedly prepared itself for US attack amid Trump’s Greenland threats</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>